What is GitOps? Let’s break it down in simple terms.

GitOps is a modern way to manage your infrastructure and deployments using Git. Here are the 4 main principles — made easy:

📝 Declarative
You write down how your system should look (like a blueprint) — and the system makes it happen.

📜 Versioned and Immutable
Every change is saved in Git. Made a mistake? Just go back to the previous version—like undoing in Google Docs.

🔄 Pulled Automatically
No more manual updates. A system watches Git and applies changes automatically when it sees a new update.

🔁 Continuously Reconciled
It keeps checking if the system is doing what’s written in Git. If something’s off—it fixes it!

✨ GitOps makes your deployments faster, safer, and easier to manage.
